== Attacks and abilities ==
{{For|strategies for defeating Seekers|Aggressive creature strategies#Seeker}}

=== Takeoff ===
When grounded between 10 and 100 meters of a player, they will launch from the ground and begin flying. This ability can be used every 8 seconds.

=== Land ===
When airborne under 5 meters of a player, they will land on the ground. This ability can be used every 8 seconds.

=== Pincers ===
Leans back before sweeping downward to clamp the player with their pincers (90 [[Damage types#Pierce|Pierce]] damage). This creates a 2.2-meter 45-degree horizontal arc and can be used every 6 seconds when within 2 meters of a player.

=== Claw ===
This attack has two variants, each with its own 10-second cooldown: a thrust with the left claw and a thrust with the right claw (120 [[Damage types#Pierce|Pierce]] damage). This hits in a 3.5-meter 20-degree horizontal arc and can be used within 3.5 meters of a player.

=== Ground slam ===
Stands on their hind legs before slamming down on the player with both claws (100 [[Damage types#Blunt|Blunt]] damage). This hits in a 3.2-meter 60-degree horizontal arc in front of Seekers and can be used every 10 seconds when within 3 meters of a player.

=== Ground slam flying ===
While airborne, leans back before propelling forward with both claws (100 [[Damage types#Blunt|Blunt]] damage). Using this attack grounds Seekers and is an alternative to landing with their Land ability. This hits in a 3.2-meter 60-degree horizontal arc in front of Seekers and can be used every 10 seconds when within 5 meters of a player.

== Notes ==
*Seekers are ant-like in appearance, but unlike ants, basic Seekers are capable of flight while Seeker Soldiers and The Queen are not.
*Seeker hives produce [[Royal Jelly]], which in real life is produced by worker bees and fed to larvae, particularly to produce new queens.

